 "about": [
  "Iinuma Meijo is a brewery in the Nishikata district of Tochigi City. It dates from 1811, when Iwajiro Iinuma, who had come from Nagaoka in Niigata to work, set up here.",
  "Its water comes from a deep well on site and is thought to be underground flow from the Oya River, which rises on Mount Nantai. The brewing follows the Niigata tōji tradition.",
  "Suginamiki, named after the cedar avenue to Nikko, is the dry label made with Tochigi rice and yeast. Sugata, named after a mirror pond in a local legend, is the more aromatic, fuller label, and also uses rice from other prefectures."
 ],
